From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rk-forge <rk-forge@localhost>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 23:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] input: goodix: release reset line after address selection

The TOPEET RK3588 GT911 stops acknowledging I2C while the reset GPIO remains
driven after the address-selection sequence.  Once the failed probe releases
the GPIO, userspace can read the controller ID again.

Both Goodix implementations in the working vendor SDK release RST to input
after T4: the board's legacy gt9xx driver and the SDK's generic Goodix driver.
Restore that board-required step while preserving the mainline timing and
interrupt synchronization sequence.

Signed-off-by: rk-forge <rk-forge@localhost>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
@@ -795,6 +795,17 @@ int goodix_reset_no_int_sync(struct goodix_ts_data *ts)
 
 	usleep_range(6000, 10000);		/* T4: > 5ms */
 
+	/*
+	 * Release the reset line after the address-selection window.  The
+	 * TOPEET vendor gt9xx driver and its generic Goodix driver both switch
+	 * RST back to input here.  Keeping RK3588 GPIO3_C1 driven caused this
+	 * panel to stop acknowledging I2C until the failed probe released the
+	 * descriptor.
+	 */
+	error = gpiod_direction_input(ts->gpiod_rst);
+	if (error)
+		goto error;
+
 	return 0;
 
 error:
